From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:23:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: decoder mode: hand the SAND buffers to the
 display

q11-063 lets the proxy hand bcm2835-codec's SAND buffer to the display
for the guest buffer it was converted into, so that weston puts a
full-screen frame on an HVS plane without the GPU. Decoder mode
(q11-069, libavcodec's v4l2request on rpi-hevc-dec) converted every
frame on the GPU and the guest composed the result, so a full-screen
HEVC frame took two GPU passes.

Offer the decoder's buffer through ui/direct-scanout.h the same way:
NV12 with the SAND128 modifier, one dma-buf, the chroma at the second
plane's offset, published for the guest buffer's texture. The display
takes it only when the guest scans that buffer out alone, full screen
and unscaled (/run/qemu-isp-scanout); otherwise the guest's copy is
shown as before. /run/qemu-sand-scanout turns the offer on.

The pixels live in libavcodec's pool, not in a buffer the guest queues,
so a frame stays showable while a reference to it is kept: from its
delivery until the guest queues its buffer again, and past that while
weston still shows it (hold). The references are bounded to 128 MiB and
2 to 32 frames, and kept only while the display takes the buffers: for
2 s after a start or after it stopped taking them, then again every
10 s. Those 2 s keep references even for a video the display does not
take -- not full screen, or a 4K frame in a 1080p window -- and the pool
keeps every buffer it has allocated until the stream stops.
direct_scanout_hit_within() is new for that. Two imports of one buffer
with different colour matrices are two entries, each with its own
reference: rare, and bounded the same way.

The pool is rpi-hevc-dec's CAPTURE queue, 32 buffers at most, and only
this thread lets its buffers go, so holding all of them would leave
v4l2request waiting for itself for good. A buffer is seen here when its
frame comes out, up to has_b_frames frames after the decoder took it;
when the (30 - has_b_frames)-th one appears, the references held then,
that frame's included, and one more become the most this pool may keep.
Past that a new reference replaces another: first one the guest is done
with and the compositor still holds (it may still be scanned out;
counted), then one not on screen (its skipped conversion is made then),
and one on screen only when all are. Should the decoder still find no
free buffer, rpidistro-ffmpeg 0002 (meta-xt-rpi5) gives up the wait
after 300 ms with ENOMEM: every reference is then let go, nothing is
offered for 10 s, the bound comes down by two, and one frame is lost
instead of the stream.

With /run/qemu-sand-skip-isp the GPU conversion itself is left out
while the display keeps taking the buffers (direct_scanout_skip_copy),
and made late from the kept frame: when the display misses (12 at
most per miss, oldest first, one wait) or before the reference to that
frame goes. A conversion or a CPU write of a guest buffer withdraws
its offer and its skipped conversion. Dropping the imports (a new
pool, size or stream, or close) forgets this owner and prints what was
offered, skipped and made late.

The display's line on the frames it did not take came every 60
misses, for good, for a window that is never taken: DomU's guest
dma-buf, 90 lines a minute. While no frame is taken the next line now
comes after twice as many misses, up to 3600 (2 lines a minute).

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c | 591 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 include/ui/direct-scanout.h      |   2 +
 ui/direct-scanout.c              |   6 +
 ui/sdl2-wl-scanout.c             |  12 +-
 4 files changed, 602 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c b/hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c
index a90f873..93d268d 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/virtio-media-decoder.c
@@ -58,6 +58,8 @@
 #include "qapi/error.h"
 #include "hw/virtio/virtio-media.h"
 #include "hw/virtio/virtio-media-virgl.h"
+#include "qemu/timer.h"
+#include "ui/direct-scanout.h"
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_VIRTIO_MEDIA_DECODER
 
@@ -150,8 +152,71 @@ typedef struct DecGpuEntry {
     uint32_t w, h;
     int matrix;
     void *handle;
+    /* q11-dec-sand-scanout: the buffer as the display sees it (dec_ds_*) */
+    int show_fd;     /* a dup of the decoder buffer's fd, or -1 */
+    uint64_t seq;    /* content generation last published for this buffer */
+    AVFrame *ref;    /* keeps the decoder off the buffer while it may be shown */
+    bool held;       /* the compositor has it on screen */
+    bool unref_on_unhold; /* the guest is done with it: let go once off screen */
 } DecGpuEntry;
 
+/*
+ * q11-dec-sand-scanout: a decoder frame is kept referenced for the display from
+ * its delivery until the guest queues its buffer again (it shows the frame in
+ * between, a couple of dozen frames later with v4l2_codec2's output delay), and
+ * past that while the compositor still has it on screen. The references are
+ * bounded as a share of the CMA the pool lives in: at most this many bytes'
+ * worth, between 2 and DEC_DS_REFS_MAX frames; beyond that one goes
+ * (dec_ds_keep says which), and that frame is shown from the guest's copy
+ * instead.
+ */
+#define DEC_DS_REFS_BYTES (128u << 20)
+#define DEC_DS_REFS_MAX 32
+/*
+ * The references cost the pool's CMA, so they are kept only while the display
+ * takes the buffers: after a start, or once it stopped taking them, for
+ * DEC_DS_PROBE_MS, and then again every DEC_DS_RETRY_MS (a video that is not
+ * full screen, or not the window's size -- a 4K one in a 1080p window -- is
+ * never taken).
+ *
+ * The limits of that probe: the pool keeps every buffer it allocated until the
+ * stream stops (v4l2request never frees one), so a probe that grew it leaves
+ * the CMA taken even when the display never took a frame; a video that goes
+ * full screen later is offered only at the next retry, up to DEC_DS_RETRY_MS
+ * on; and "the display takes" is any producer's buffer within the last second
+ * (direct_scanout_hit_within), not only this decoder's.
+ */
+#define DEC_DS_PROBE_MS 2000
+#define DEC_DS_RETRY_MS 10000
+/*
+ * libavcodec's pool is rpi-hevc-dec's CAPTURE queue, which takes VB2_MAX_FRAME
+ * (32) buffers and no more. Past that v4l2request waits for a buffer to come
+ * free, and only this thread frees them: with every buffer referenced here
+ * that wait would never end (rpidistro-ffmpeg 0002 bounds it, dec_ds_starved).
+ * The pool grows only when no buffer is free, and a buffer is seen here only
+ * when its frame comes out, up to has_b_frames frames after it was taken. So
+ * when the import of the (DEC_DS_POOL_SOFT - has_b_frames)-th buffer appears,
+ * every buffer of the DEC_DS_POOL_SOFT is in use, and the references held then
+ * plus one more is how many the pool has room for: they are not let grow past
+ * that (ds_refs_cap) for as long as the pool lives, which leaves the last
+ * buffer for the decoder's own references varying. Should the decoder run out
+ * even so (dec_ds_starved), the bound comes down by two. (The Raspberry Pi 5,
+ * HEVC 1080p60 with has_b_frames 2: set at the 28th import, 26 frames. With
+ * the held references alone, 23 or 24 at that point, a bound of 24 let frames
+ * the compositor still held go, 25 did not.)
+ */
+#define DEC_POOL_MAX 32
+#define DEC_DS_POOL_SOFT (DEC_POOL_MAX - 2)
+/* Skipped conversions one catch-up makes at most, oldest first. */
+#define DEC_DS_CATCH_MAX 12
+
+/* q11-dec-sand-scanout: a guest buffer whose copy was skipped, for the catch-up */
+typedef struct DecDsPend {
+    uint32_t res;
+    unsigned slot;
+    uint64_t seq;
+} DecDsPend;
+
 /* A blitted hardware frame and the import whose GPU work reads it. */
 typedef struct DecGpuHeld {
     AVFrame *frame;
@@ -270,6 +335,25 @@ struct VirtIOMediaDec {
     unsigned gpu_n;
     DecGpuHeld gpu_held[DEC_GPU_HOLD];
     unsigned gpu_held_n;
+
+    /*
+     * q11-dec-sand-scanout: the decoder's SAND buffers handed to the display
+     * (ui/direct-scanout.h) for the guest buffer they were blitted into, so
+     * that a full-screen frame goes on a plane without the conversion.
+     */
+    uint64_t ds_epoch;                /* 0: nothing published since the last clear */
+    uint64_t ds_seq;
+    unsigned ds_fifo[DEC_GPU_CACHE];  /* slots holding a reference, oldest first */
+    unsigned ds_refs;
+    unsigned ds_refs_cap;             /* per gpu_fctx; 0: not set yet */
+    DecDsPend ds_pend[VIRTIO_MEDIA_MAX_BUFFERS]; /* oldest first */
+    unsigned ds_pend_n;
+    unsigned ds_by_buf[VIRTIO_MEDIA_MAX_BUFFERS]; /* guest capture buffer -> slot + 1 */
+    int64_t ds_probe_ms; /* when offering without the display taking began, 0: it takes */
+    int64_t ds_backoff_ms; /* no offers before this (dec_ds_starved) */
+    bool ds_logged;
+    uint64_t ds_pub_n, ds_skip_n, ds_catch_n, ds_lost_n, ds_evict_held_n;
+    uint64_t ds_starved_n, ds_evict_release_n;
 };
 
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
@@ -474,10 +558,14 @@ static void dec_gpu_unhold_oldest(VirtIOMediaDec *d)
             d->gpu_held_n * sizeof(d->gpu_held[0]));
 }
 
+static void dec_ds_drop(VirtIOMediaDec *d);
+
 static void dec_gpu_clear(VirtIOMediaDec *d)
 {
     unsigned i;
 
+    /* the display's references and fds name these entries' slots */
+    dec_ds_drop(d);
     /* the held frames' waits use the imports, so they go first */
     while (d->gpu_held_n) {
         dec_gpu_unhold_oldest(d);
@@ -497,6 +585,7 @@ static void dec_gpu_reset(VirtIOMediaDec *d)
 {
     dec_gpu_clear(d);
     av_buffer_unref(&d->gpu_fctx);
+    d->ds_refs_cap = 0;
     d->gpu_off = false;
     d->gpu_again = 0;
 }
@@ -533,6 +622,404 @@ static void dec_gpu_hold(VirtIOMediaDec *d, const AVFrame *fr, void *handle)
     d->gpu_held_n++;
 }
 
+/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
+/* q11-dec-sand-scanout: the decoder's buffers straight to the display        */
+/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
+
+/*
+ * The proxy (q11-063) hands the display bcm2835-codec's SAND buffer for the
+ * guest buffer it was converted into, so that weston puts a full-screen frame
+ * on an HVS plane; this is the same for the decoder's (v4l2request) buffers.
+ * The display (ui/sdl2-gl.c, sdl2-wl-scanout.c) takes the buffer instead of the
+ * guest's copy only when the guest scans that copy out full screen and alone
+ * (/run/qemu-isp-scanout); otherwise the copy is shown as before.
+ *
+ * Unlike the proxy's, the pixels live in libavcodec's pool, not in a buffer the
+ * guest queues: a frame stays showable while a reference to it is kept, and the
+ * pool grows by the references (dec_ds_keep bounds them) and does not shrink
+ * back until the stream stops. With
+ * /run/qemu-sand-skip-isp the conversion itself is skipped while the display
+ * keeps taking the buffer (direct_scanout_skip_copy), and made late, from the
+ * kept reference, when it stops (dec_ds_catch_up).
+ */
+static bool dec_ds_file_on(const char *path, int64_t *checked, bool *on)
+{
+    int64_t now = qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME);
+
+    if (now - *checked >= 1000) {
+        *checked = now;
+        *on = access(path, F_OK) == 0;
+    }
+    return *on;
+}
+
+static bool dec_ds_on(void)
+{
+    static int64_t checked = -1000000;
+    static bool on;
+
+    return dec_ds_file_on("/run/qemu-sand-scanout", &checked, &on);
+}
+
+static bool dec_ds_skip_on(void)
+{
+    static int64_t checked = -1000000;
+    static bool on;
+
+    return dec_ds_file_on("/run/qemu-sand-skip-isp", &checked, &on);
+}
+
+static uint64_t dec_ds_epochs;
+
+static bool dec_ds_current(void *owner, uint32_t slot, uint64_t seq)
+{
+    VirtIOMediaDec *d = owner;
+
+    return slot < d->gpu_n && d->gpu[slot].ref && d->gpu[slot].seq == seq;
+}
+
+static void dec_ds_unref(VirtIOMediaDec *d, unsigned slot);
+
+static void dec_ds_hold(void *owner, uint32_t slot, bool held)
+{
+    VirtIOMediaDec *d = owner;
+
+    if (slot >= d->gpu_n) {
+        return;
+    }
+    d->gpu[slot].held = held;
+    if (!held && d->gpu[slot].unref_on_unhold) {
+        dec_ds_unref(d, slot);
+    }
+}
+
+static void dec_ds_pend_remove(VirtIOMediaDec *d, unsigned i)
+{
+    d->ds_pend_n--;
+    memmove(&d->ds_pend[i], &d->ds_pend[i + 1],
+            (d->ds_pend_n - i) * sizeof(d->ds_pend[0]));
+}
+
+/*
+ * The reference to slot's frame is about to go: a conversion skipped from it is
+ * made now, while the frame is still there, or the guest's copy stays stale.
+ */
+static void dec_ds_settle_slot(VirtIOMediaDec *d, unsigned slot)
+{
+    unsigned i = 0;
+
+    while (i < d->ds_pend_n) {
+        DecDsPend *p = &d->ds_pend[i];
+
+        if (p->slot != slot) {
+            i++;
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (dec_ds_current(d, slot, p->seq) &&
+            virtio_media_gpu_blit(d->gpu[slot].handle, p->res) == 0) {
+            /* the decoder must not write the buffer before the GPU read it */
+            dec_gpu_hold(d, d->gpu[slot].ref, d->gpu[slot].handle);
+            d->ds_catch_n++;
+        } else {
+            d->ds_lost_n++;
+        }
+        dec_ds_pend_remove(d, i);
+    }
+}
+
+static void dec_ds_unref(VirtIOMediaDec *d, unsigned slot)
+{
+    unsigned i;
+
+    dec_ds_settle_slot(d, slot);
+    av_frame_free(&d->gpu[slot].ref);
+    d->gpu[slot].unref_on_unhold = false;
+    for (i = 0; i < VIRTIO_MEDIA_MAX_BUFFERS; i++) {
+        if (d->ds_by_buf[i] == slot + 1) {
+            d->ds_by_buf[i] = 0;
+        }
+    }
+    for (i = 0; i < d->ds_refs; i++) {
+        if (d->ds_fifo[i] == slot) {
+            d->ds_refs--;
+            memmove(&d->ds_fifo[i], &d->ds_fifo[i + 1],
+                    (d->ds_refs - i) * sizeof(d->ds_fifo[0]));
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/* Frames of this many bytes kept at most (DEC_DS_REFS_BYTES), 2 at least. */
+static unsigned dec_ds_max_refs(size_t bytes)
+{
+    size_t n = bytes ? DEC_DS_REFS_BYTES / bytes : DEC_DS_REFS_MAX;
+
+    return (unsigned)MAX(MIN(n, (size_t)DEC_DS_REFS_MAX), (size_t)2);
+}
+
+/*
+ * The guest queued capture buffer index again: it is done with the frame it
+ * showed from it, so the decoder may have that buffer back, once off screen.
+ */
+static void dec_ds_unpend(VirtIOMediaDec *d, uint32_t res);
+
+static void dec_ds_requeued(VirtIOMediaDec *d, unsigned index, uint32_t res)
+{
+    unsigned slot;
+
+    /* the buffer's next content comes from the decoder: nothing to catch up */
+    dec_ds_unpend(d, res);
+    if (index >= VIRTIO_MEDIA_MAX_BUFFERS || !d->ds_by_buf[index]) {
+        return;
+    }
+    slot = d->ds_by_buf[index] - 1;
+    d->ds_by_buf[index] = 0;
+    if (slot >= d->gpu_n) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (d->gpu[slot].held) {
+        d->gpu[slot].unref_on_unhold = true;
+    } else {
+        dec_ds_unref(d, slot);
+    }
+}
+
+/* Keep fr (in slot) showable for guest buffer index, within the bound. */
+static bool dec_ds_keep(VirtIOMediaDec *d, unsigned slot, unsigned index,
+                        const AVFrame *fr, size_t bytes, int reorder)
+{
+    DecGpuEntry *e = &d->gpu[slot];
+    unsigned max = dec_ds_max_refs(bytes);
+    unsigned soft = DEC_DS_POOL_SOFT - (unsigned)MIN(MAX(reorder, 0), 16);
+
+    /*
+     * Normally a no-op: the decoder could write fr into this buffer only once
+     * its last reference was gone, so slot has no reference, and any skipped
+     * conversion from it was settled then; its seq is still the old content's,
+     * which makes nothing current here.
+     */
+    dec_ds_unref(d, slot);
+    if (!d->ds_refs_cap && d->gpu_n >= soft) {
+        /* fr, in the buffer that just appeared, is one of them; one more */
+        d->ds_refs_cap = d->ds_refs + 2;
+        info_report("virtio-media/dec: sand-scanout: %u of the decoder's "
+                    "buffers seen, up to %d more decoded ahead: keeping %u "
+                    "frames at most", d->gpu_n, reorder, d->ds_refs_cap);
+    }
+    if (d->ds_refs_cap) {
+        /* near the end of the pool: replace one, do not add */
+        max = MIN(max, d->ds_refs_cap);
+    }
+    while (d->ds_refs && d->ds_refs >= max) {
+        unsigned i, pick = 0;
+
+        /*
+         * Which frame goes. First the oldest one the guest is done with and
+         * the compositor still holds: most likely a newer frame has replaced
+         * it and it waits for its release, but it may still be scanned out
+         * (counted apart). Then the oldest one not on screen;
+         * the guest has still to show that one, so the display misses it and
+         * the skipped conversion of it is made now (dec_ds_settle_slot).
+         * The oldest of all only when every frame is on screen (counted, as
+         * the proxy does: it may be written over while shown).
+         */
+        for (i = 0; i < d->ds_refs; i++) {
+            if (d->gpu[d->ds_fifo[i]].unref_on_unhold) {
+                pick = i;
+                d->ds_evict_release_n++;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+        if (i == d->ds_refs) {
+            for (i = 0; i < d->ds_refs && d->gpu[d->ds_fifo[i]].held; i++) {
+            }
+            if (i < d->ds_refs) {
+                pick = i;
+            } else {
+                d->ds_evict_held_n++;
+            }
+        }
+        dec_ds_unref(d, d->ds_fifo[pick]);
+    }
+    e->ref = av_frame_alloc();
+    if (!e->ref || av_frame_ref(e->ref, fr) < 0) {
+        av_frame_free(&e->ref);
+        return false;
+    }
+    /* a new generation: older offers of this buffer are stale from now */
+    e->seq = ++d->ds_seq;
+    d->ds_fifo[d->ds_refs++] = slot;
+    if (index < VIRTIO_MEDIA_MAX_BUFFERS) {
+        d->ds_by_buf[index] = slot + 1;
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Let every kept frame go (the display does not take them): the decoder may
+ * reuse the buffers. The pool does not shrink; it only stops growing.
+ */
+static void dec_ds_release(VirtIOMediaDec *d)
+{
+    unsigned i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < d->gpu_n; i++) {
+        if (!d->gpu[i].ref) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (d->gpu[i].held) {
+            d->gpu[i].unref_on_unhold = true;
+        } else {
+            dec_ds_unref(d, i);
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/* Offer the decoder's buffers now? See DEC_DS_PROBE_MS. */
+static bool dec_ds_wanted(VirtIOMediaDec *d)
+{
+    int64_t now = qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME);
+
+    if (now < d->ds_backoff_ms) {
+        dec_ds_release(d);
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (direct_scanout_hit_within(1000)) {
+        d->ds_probe_ms = 0;
+        return true;
+    }
+    if (!d->ds_probe_ms || now - d->ds_probe_ms >= DEC_DS_RETRY_MS) {
+        d->ds_probe_ms = now;
+    }
+    if (now - d->ds_probe_ms < DEC_DS_PROBE_MS) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    dec_ds_release(d);
+    return false;
+}
+
+/* The guest buffer res got its content by the conversion: nothing to catch up. */
+static void dec_ds_unpend(VirtIOMediaDec *d, uint32_t res)
+{
+    unsigned i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < d->ds_pend_n; i++) {
+        if (d->ds_pend[i].res == res) {
+            dec_ds_pend_remove(d, i);
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/*
+ * The display missed: make the skipped conversions, oldest first (the guest
+ * shows them in that order), DEC_DS_CATCH_MAX at most so that one miss does not
+ * stop the main loop for a whole queue's worth; the next miss makes the rest.
+ * The blits are on one GL context, so the GPU runs them in order and the last
+ * one's fence covers the others: one wait.
+ */
+static void dec_ds_catch_up(void *owner)
+{
+    VirtIOMediaDec *d = owner;
+    void *last = NULL;
+    unsigned n;
+
+    for (n = 0; d->ds_pend_n && n < DEC_DS_CATCH_MAX; n++) {
+        DecDsPend p = d->ds_pend[0];
+
+        dec_ds_pend_remove(d, 0);
+        if (dec_ds_current(d, p.slot, p.seq) &&
+            virtio_media_gpu_blit(d->gpu[p.slot].handle, p.res) == 0) {
+            last = d->gpu[p.slot].handle;
+            d->ds_catch_n++;
+        } else {
+            d->ds_lost_n++; /* the blit failed: the guest's copy is stale */
+        }
+    }
+    if (last && virtio_media_gpu_wait(last) < 0) {
+        warn_report_once("virtio-media/dec: host-sand: GPU wait failed");
+    }
+}
+
+/* Every entry goes (dec_gpu_clear): the display forgets this owner's buffers. */
+static void dec_ds_drop(VirtIOMediaDec *d)
+{
+    unsigned i;
+
+    if (d->ds_epoch) {
+        direct_scanout_forget(d);
+        d->ds_epoch = 0;
+    }
+    if (d->ds_pub_n) {
+        info_report("virtio-media/dec: sand-scanout: %" PRIu64 " offered, %"
+                    PRIu64 " conversions skipped, %" PRIu64 " made late, %"
+                    PRIu64 " lost, %u still skipped at the stop, %" PRIu64
+                    " let go before their release, %" PRIu64 " evicted on "
+                    "screen, %" PRIu64 " pool waits given up", d->ds_pub_n,
+                    d->ds_skip_n, d->ds_catch_n, d->ds_lost_n, d->ds_pend_n,
+                    d->ds_evict_release_n, d->ds_evict_held_n, d->ds_starved_n);
+        d->ds_pub_n = d->ds_skip_n = d->ds_catch_n = d->ds_lost_n = 0;
+        d->ds_evict_held_n = d->ds_starved_n = d->ds_evict_release_n = 0;
+    }
+    for (i = 0; i < d->gpu_n; i++) {
+        DecGpuEntry *e = &d->gpu[i];
+
+        av_frame_free(&e->ref);
+        e->held = false;
+        e->unref_on_unhold = false;
+        if (e->show_fd >= 0) {
+            close(e->show_fd);
+            e->show_fd = -1;
+        }
+    }
+    d->ds_refs = 0;
+    d->ds_pend_n = 0;
+    d->ds_probe_ms = 0;
+    memset(d->ds_by_buf, 0, sizeof(d->ds_by_buf));
+}
+
+/*
+ * libavcodec failed a frame with ENOMEM: with rpidistro-ffmpeg 0002 that is
+ * v4l2request giving up its wait for a free destination buffer, and only the
